            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Oxalis brasiliensis, also known by its common name Brazilian woodsorrel is a species from the section Ionoxalis. It was first described by Dámaso Antonio Larrañaga."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Description\nOxalis brasiliensis is a herbaceous, perennial plant with a very long but simple root and very small stems. It has yellow or brilliant crimson-purple flowers."
          }
